{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:1-rite", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (rite)"}, "paraphrase": "One who renounces in due order performs the Vaiśvānara sacrifice, places the fires in himself, tells his son 'you are the sacrifice, you are all' (or without a son departs east or north), begs among the three higher varṇas, uses the hand as bowl, stays one night in a village, five in a town, four months in the rains; his thread is meditation on the Self, his topknot knowledge; for him there is no night or day.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite", "cpt:inner-sikha-yajnopavita"], "practices": ["prc:sannyasa-diksa", "prc:parivrajya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.1-5", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.1-5"}, "paraphrase": "After the forty saṃskāras, one who has dispassion may renounce; three are called fallen — who makes a renouncer fall, who makes a fallen one renounce, who obstructs renunciation; the ineligible (including the leprous and the unbelieving) may renounce only when sick unto death.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-may-renounce"], "disputes": ["dsp:who-may-renounce"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.101", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.101"}, "paraphrase": "Activity is of two kinds, 'of the cat' and 'of the monkey'; the text assigns them to those devoted to knowledge and practice (construal uncertain).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.103-104", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.103-104"}, "paraphrase": "One who repeats twelve thousand praṇavas daily sees Brahman shine within twelve months.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.12", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.12"}, "paraphrase": "'Abandon dharma and adharma, abandon truth and untruth; having abandoned both, abandon that by which you abandon.'", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.13-58", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.13-58"}, "paraphrase": "Verses on the knower (many shared with the Yoga Vāsiṣṭha): freedom from vāsanā, equanimity, the mind's dissolution.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.59-64", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.59-64"}, "paraphrase": "Food: fill half the stomach with food, a quarter with water, leave a quarter for air; fasting is better than eating at night, unsolicited food better than fasting, alms better than unsolicited food.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "practices": ["prc:mitahara", "prc:madhukari-bhiksa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.6-8", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.6-8"}, "paraphrase": "When the sun sees a renouncer it trembles, thinking 'he will pierce my orb'; one who renounces saves sixty generations before and after; the fire of the renunciation declaration burns faults.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.65-71", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.65-71"}, "paraphrase": "Five kinds of alms: mādhūkara (a little from several houses like a bee), prākpraṇīta (arranged in advance), ayācita (unasked), tātkālika (what comes at the moment) and upapanna (brought to him); mādhūkara may be taken even from a mleccha, never food from a single house.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-kinds-of-alms"], "practices": ["prc:madhukari-bhiksa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.74-76", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.74-76"}, "paraphrase": "He avoids food from the accused, the fallen, heretics and temple priests; ghee is like dog's urine to him.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.79-85", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.79-85"}, "paraphrase": "Six things bind a renouncer: a fixed seat (staying beyond the rains), losing his bowl, hoarding, gathering disciples for service, gain, worship or fame (not out of compassion), sleep (negligence in study) and idle talk.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "obstacles": ["obs:renouncer-causes-of-fall"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.9-11", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.9-11"}, "paraphrase": "The staff is of bamboo, smooth, of prescribed measure; he should never go three arrow-shots without it.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:renunciant-marks"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.91", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.91"}, "paraphrase": "Six things he must never accept: immovable property, movables, seed, metal vessels, poison and weapons.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.97", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.97"}, "paraphrase": "Tridaṇḍa means three restraints: silence the staff of speech, not eating (desire-less eating) the staff of body, breath-control the staff of mind.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:renunciant-marks"], "disputes": ["dsp:renunciant-marks-ekadanda-tridanda"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sannyasa-upanisad:2.98-100", "source": "src:sannyasa-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.98-100"}, "paraphrase": "Beings are bound by action and freed by knowledge; streets full of rags, alms everywhere, the earth a wide bed — why should ascetics be unhappy? One who offers the world into the fire of knowledge is the true agnihotrin.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-sacrifice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
